From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] pan/bi: update LCRA constraints after spilling instead of rebuilding them, spill in one scan biblioklept

After each spill round, register allocation rebuilt liveness and every
interference constraint from scratch, though spilling only touches the
spilled nodes and adds fill temporaries.

Spilling a node keeps its definitions, adds stores of it and fills into
new temporaries, and rewrites only its own sources. Every other node's
liveness is unchanged, so the constraints between two other nodes are
too. The constraint state now grows to the new node count, drops the
spilled nodes' constraints, and an interference pass over the shader
records only the constraints that involve a spilled or new node (clean
definitions walk only the live "dirty" nodes). Affinities and forced
registers are redone for those nodes.

The spilled nodes of a round are also spilled from one scan of the
shader: the instructions referencing each node (or defining its spill
point) are collected first, then each node is spilled in turn exactly
as before, so fills get the same temporaries in the same order.

Output is identical on all 67539 corpus shaders. Host, 18 NFS-range
synthetic shaders: 472 -> 345 ms, RA 348 -> 218 ms; 65 very large
synthetic shaders: 13.8 -> 8.0 s.
---
diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_ra.c
